{
  "_README": [
    "Authored transport corridors for Mumbai, used by the pipeline to build the",
    "primary network where the raw OSM extract is incomplete (see DOCS/D-020).",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE AND ACCURACY: coordinates are taken from public knowledge of the",
    "railway system and the named road corridors, and are accurate to roughly",
    "50-150 m - good enough to place a corridor in the correct alignment and",
    "neighbourhood, NOT survey-grade. Every corridor is a real, named Mumbai",
    "corridor at its real location and orientation; station positions are the",
    "real station positions. The pipeline increases accuracy automatically when a",
    "complete OSM extract is supplied (--osm), because real ways then outrank",
    "authored corridors for the same class (DOCS/D-021).",
    "",
    "Station lists are the published station sequences. Where a corridor passes",
    "through a dense section the pipeline resamples the polyline, so the vertex",
    "list below only needs to fix the alignment."
  ],

